{
  "slug": "pronombres",
  "number": 15,
  "part": 4,
  "title": "Object pronouns",
  "tagline": "Le, la, les, lui, leur: where they go and how to choose. Plus moi, toi, lui…",
  "goal": "Replace people and things with le, la, les, lui and leur, put them in the right place and use the stressed pronouns moi, toi, lui…",
  "minutes": 12,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "para-que",
      "title": "What they're for",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To avoid repeating yourself, like «it» or «them» in English. The big difference: in French the pronoun goes **before the verb**."
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            {
              "fr": "J'adore la pizza. Je la mange tous les jours.",
              "tr": "I love pizza. I eat it every day. (literally «I it eat»)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The pronouns *en* and *y* have their own module [[16]]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cod",
      "title": "Direct object: le, la, les",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The **direct object** (COD) answers «what?» or «who?» and follows the verb **with no preposition**."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Pronoun",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "me",
              "*me / m'*",
              "*Il m'aime.*"
            ],
            [
              "you (tu)",
              "*te / t'*",
              "*Je {te} vois.*"
            ],
            [
              "him, it / her, it",
              "*le / la / l'*",
              "*Je {le} regarde. · Tu {la} connais.*"
            ],
            [
              "us",
              "*nous*",
              "*Elle {nous} invite.*"
            ],
            [
              "you (vous)",
              "*vous*",
              "*Je {vous} écoute.*"
            ],
            [
              "them",
              "*les*",
              "*Il {les} mange.*"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "*le* and *la* also mean «it», depending on the gender of the thing: *la pizza* → *je la mange*. Before a vowel or silent h, they become *l'*: *Je l'aime.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "coi",
      "title": "Indirect object: lui, leur",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The **indirect object** (COI) is a person introduced by **à** (to): *parler à, téléphoner à, donner à, dire à, écrire à, répondre à*…"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Pronoun",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(to) me",
              "*me / m'*",
              "*Il {me} parle.*"
            ],
            [
              "(to) you (tu)",
              "*te / t'*",
              "*Je {te} téléphone.*"
            ],
            [
              "(to) him, (to) her",
              "*lui*",
              "*Je {lui} écris.*"
            ],
            [
              "(to) us",
              "*nous*",
              "*Tu {nous} réponds.*"
            ],
            [
              "(to) you (vous)",
              "*vous*",
              "*Je {vous} dis bonjour.*"
            ],
            [
              "(to) them",
              "*leur*",
              "*Elle {leur} donne un cadeau.*"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "*lui* means «to him» **and** «to her»: *Je parle à Marie* → *Je lui parle*."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "text": "Don't confuse the pronoun *leur* (never takes an s) with the possessive *leur / leurs* [[8]]: *Je leur parle* (I speak to them) vs *C'est leur maison* (It's their house)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test",
      "title": "Direct or indirect?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Look at the **French** verb: does it take **à** before the person?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": [
            "Is there à?",
            "Type",
            "Example",
            "With a pronoun"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "No",
              "COD",
              "*Je regarde Paul.*",
              "*Je le regarde.*"
            ],
            [
              "Yes",
              "COI",
              "*Je parle à Paul.*",
              "*Je lui parle.*"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "English can mislead you",
          "text": "Some verbs take a preposition in English but not in French: *écouter* (listen to), *attendre* (wait for), *regarder* (look at), *chercher* (look for) are direct: *J'attends le bus* → *Je l'attends*. And the reverse: «call someone» is *téléphoner à quelqu'un* → *Je lui téléphone*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posicion",
      "title": "Where they go",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": [
            "Situation",
            "Position",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**Present**",
              "before the verb",
              "*Je la regarde.*"
            ],
            [
              "**Negative**",
              "between *ne* and the verb",
              "*Je ne la regarde pas.*"
            ],
            [
              "**Verb + infinitive**",
              "before the infinitive",
              "*Je vais la regarder. · Je veux lui parler.*"
            ],
            [
              "**Passé composé**",
              "before the auxiliary",
              "*Je l'ai regardée. · Je lui ai parlé.*"
            ],
            [
              "**Positive imperative**",
              "after, with a hyphen",
              "*Regarde-la ! · Parle-lui !*"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "title": "Agreement with avoir",
          "text": "In the *passé composé* with *avoir*, if the direct object comes **before**, the participle agrees with it: *J'ai mangé la pizza* → *Je l'ai mangée*. Not with the indirect object: *Je lui ai parlé*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tonicos",
      "title": "Stressed pronouns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": [
            "je",
            "tu",
            "il",
            "elle",
            "nous",
            "vous",
            "ils",
            "elles"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "*moi*",
              "*toi*",
              "*lui*",
              "*elle*",
              "*nous*",
              "*vous*",
              "*eux*",
              "*elles*"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "For **emphasis**: *Moi, j'adore le fromage.* (Me, I love cheese.)",
            "After a **preposition**: *avec toi, chez moi, pour eux, sans elle*.",
            "In **short answers**: *Qui veut du café ? — Moi !*",
            "With *aussi* and *non plus*: *Moi aussi* (me too) · *Moi non plus* (me neither).",
            "After *c'est*: *C'est lui !* (It's him!)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "cod-coi",
      "title": "Le or lui?",
      "instructions": "Replace Sophie with the right pronoun.",
      "kind": "choice",
      "options": [
        "l'",
        "la",
        "lui"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "prompt": "J'aide Sophie. → Je ___ aide.",
          "answer": "l'",
          "explain": "*aider* takes no à: direct object."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Je donne un livre à Sophie. → Je ___ donne un livre.",
          "answer": "lui"
        },
        {
          "prompt": "J'écoute Sophie. → Je ___ écoute.",
          "answer": "l'",
          "explain": "«Listen to» but *écouter* takes no à."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Je réponds à Sophie. → Je ___ réponds.",
          "answer": "lui"
        },
        {
          "prompt": "J'appelle Sophie. → Je ___ appelle.",
          "answer": "l'",
          "explain": "*appeler* takes no à: direct object."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Je dis bonjour à Sophie. → Je ___ dis bonjour.",
          "answer": "lui"
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Je vois Sophie demain. → Je ___ vois demain.",
          "answer": "la"
        }
      ],
      "section": "test"
    },
